# rag-api workflow diagrams
#
# Render with Mermaid-compatible tools (GitHub Markdown, Mermaid Live Editor,
# VS Code Mermaid extensions, or documentation platforms supporting Mermaid).

## 1. System components

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    Client[Client / AI platform] --> API[FastAPI application]
    API --> TM[MultiTenantRAGManager]
    TM --> LI[Tenant LightRAG instance]
    API --> PARSE[Parser selection and task processing]
    PARSE --> DIRECT[Direct text insertion]
    PARSE --> DOC[Docling]
    PARSE --> MINERU[MinerU]
    PARSE --> OCR[DeepSeek-OCR]
    DOC --> RA[RAG-Anything]
    MINERU --> RA
    DIRECT --> LI
    OCR --> LI
    RA --> LI
    LI --> KV[(DragonflyDB / Redis-compatible KV)]
    LI --> V[(Qdrant vector database)]
    LI --> G[(Memgraph graph database)]
    LI --> STATUS[(Document status storage)]
```

## 2. Lazy tenant instance creation

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    R[Request includes tenant_id] --> M[MultiTenantRAGManager]
    M --> C{Instance already cached?}
    C -- Yes --> RET[Return cached LightRAG instance]
    C -- No --> CFG[Load tenant configuration and global defaults]
    CFG --> NEW[Construct LightRAG with tenant workspace]
    NEW --> INIT[Initialize storage components]
    INIT --> CACHE[Cache instance]
    CACHE --> RET
```

## 3. Document ingestion and extraction

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[POST /insert: tenant_id, doc_id, file, parser options] --> B[Validate upload]
    B --> C[Stage file temporarily]
    C --> D[Create task record and return task_id]
    D --> E[Background document processing]
    E --> F[Get or create tenant LightRAG instance]
    F --> P{Select extraction path}
    P -->|Text / Markdown / supported text-like file| TXT[Read text directly]
    P -->|Docling| DOC[Docling conversion]
    P -->|Local MinerU| ML[MinerU local parsing]
    P -->|Remote MinerU| MR[Remote MinerU service]
    P -->|DeepSeek-OCR| OCR[OCR client / model]
    DOC --> RA[RAG-Anything processing]
    ML --> RA
    MR --> RP[Process remote MinerU result]
    TXT --> INS[Send content to LightRAG]
    OCR --> INS
    RA --> INS
    RP --> INS
    INS --> IDX[Chunking, embeddings, entity/relation extraction]
    IDX --> STORES[(KV + Vector + Graph storage)]
    STORES --> CLEAN[Temporary upload cleanup]
    CLEAN --> DONE[Task status reconciled with document status]
```

## 4. LightRAG indexing

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    CONTENT[Extracted text / supported multimodal content] --> CHUNK[Prepare and split into chunks]
    CHUNK --> KV[Persist chunk text and metadata in KV storage]
    CHUNK --> EMB[Generate chunk embeddings]
    EMB --> Q1[(Qdrant: chunk vectors)]
    CHUNK --> LLM[LLM extracts entities and relationships]
    LLM --> MERGE[Merge / update entity and relation information]
    MERGE --> GRAPH[(Memgraph: graph nodes and edges)]
    MERGE --> EREMB[Generate entity and relationship embeddings]
    EREMB --> Q2[(Qdrant: entity and relation vectors)]
    CHUNK --> SRC[Maintain document / source associations]
    SRC --> KV
```

## 5. Query workflow (conceptual mix mode)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Q[User question] --> PREP[Query preparation / keyword extraction]
    PREP --> QD[(Qdrant)]
    QD --> EH[Entity vector hits]
    QD --> RH[Relationship vector hits]
    QD --> CH[Chunk vector hits]
    EH --> MG[(Memgraph)]
    RH --> MG
    MG --> GR[Relevant graph nodes and edges]
    CH --> KV[(DragonflyDB / KV)]
    GR --> KV
    KV --> CTX[Fetch source chunk text and assemble context]
    CTX --> LLM[Query LLM]
    LLM --> ANS[Answer]
```

## 6. Roles of the three main databases

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Q[Question / search terms] --> V[(Qdrant)]
    V -->|Candidate vector IDs| G[(Memgraph)]
    G -->|Graph nodes, edges, descriptions| K[(DragonflyDB / KV)]
    V -->|Relevant chunk IDs| K
    K -->|Original text passages| C[Context assembly]
    G --> C
    C --> L[LLM]
    L --> A[Answer]
```

## 7. Task status lifecycle

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Pending
    Pending --> Processing
    Processing --> Completed
    Processing --> Failed
    Completed --> [*]
    Failed --> [*]
```
